      "message": "fix(post): Tormach states the clearance Z before the first X/Y traverse\n\nAfter a tool change (or a G30, or at the program start) tormach.cps\nnow writes G0 Z<ClearancePlane> (else the RetractPlane, never below the\nmove's own Z) before an upright section's first X/Y traverse, and\nrefuses by name a stream that states neither plane. The top of Z\ntravel is not proof of clearance: in a PathPilot Hub run a 5\" T4 on a\nhigh G54 Z zero stood 0.68\" under the part top after G43, and the bare\nX/Y rapid crossed the part. With the height stated, a setup that cannot\nclear is stopped by the control's Z limit instead.\n\n32 Tormach goldens gain that one G0 Z line; the hand-written test\nstreams state the clearance plane a real section carries. The other\nmill posts are #1616.\n\nFixes #1614\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
